1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:04,200

What if all the oxygen vanished?

2
00:00:04,200 --> 00:00:08,000

A calm Sunday evening on the Sarawak River.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:11,600

Kuching. People stroll the waterfront.

4
00:00:11,600 --> 00:00:16,200

In thirty seconds, every oxygen atom on Earth will vanish.

5
00:00:16,200 --> 00:00:20,200

Oxygen is 21% of this air...

6
00:00:20,200 --> 00:00:24,800

...89% of every drop of river water...

7
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:28,400

...53% of every window...

8
00:00:28,400 --> 00:00:32,400

...about 65% of every person here...

9
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:36,400

...and almost half the ground beneath them.

10
00:00:36,400 --> 00:00:41,600

Nobody here knows.

11
00:00:41,600 --> 00:00:43,800

T = 0

12
00:00:43,800 --> 00:00:47,800

Every window is gone. Glass is 53% oxygen.

13
00:00:47,800 --> 00:00:52,100

So is the river. Water minus oxygen is hydrogen gas.

14
00:00:52,100 --> 00:00:55,700

One millisecond later, everyone here pops.

15
00:00:55,700 --> 00:00:59,900

Their leftover hydrogen was packed at over 1,000 atmospheres.

16
00:00:59,900 --> 00:01:04,300

The river's hydrogen blasts upward. No fire. Just pressure.

17
00:01:04,300 --> 00:01:08,100

Concrete is mostly oxides. It turns to powder.

18
00:01:08,100 --> 00:01:13,690

A 50-metre tower has nothing left to hold it up. It falls in 3.2 seconds.

19
00:01:13,690 --> 00:01:16,890

Only the steel stands.

20
00:01:16,890 --> 00:01:20,090

Engines stop. Nothing can burn.

21
00:01:20,090 --> 00:01:23,290

T + 10 seconds. Silence.

22
00:01:23,290 --> 00:01:28,300

Air pressure: 0.77 atmospheres. Your ears would pop, if you still had ears.

23
00:01:28,300 --> 00:01:33,310

Above it all, a sky of hydrogen. Flammable. Nothing left to light it.

24
00:01:33,310 --> 00:01:36,910

Same second, everywhere on Earth.

25
00:01:37,710 --> 00:01:42,110
The mass of today's air
Every sea becomes sky.

26
00:01:42,110 --> 00:01:46,110

The ozone layer is oxygen too. UV protection: cancelled.

27
00:01:46,110 --> 00:01:50,780
About 24 moons
Earth is still here. Just a lot less of it.

28
00:01:50,780 --> 00:01:55,510

The Sun is 0.57% oxygen. It keeps shining. Earth stays in orbit.

29
00:01:55,510 --> 00:01:59,710

Mars stops being red. Europa loses its hidden ocean.

30
00:01:59,710 --> 00:02:04,510

Hydrogen: Earth flies away. Oxygen: Earth stays, and crumbles. Pick your apocalypse.

31
00:02:05,310 --> 00:02:11,310

What if all the oxygen vanished?

32
00:02:11,310 --> 00:02:14,710

Which element should we delete next?

